  "solution": "<p>For <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>&#x02264;</mo><mi>r</mi><mo>&#x02264;</mo><mn>44</mn></mrow></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>tan</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>&#x02218;</mo></msup><mi>tan</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00028;</mo><mn>90</mn><mo>&#x02212;</mo><mi>r</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">&#x00029;</mo><mo>&#x02218;</mo></msup><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>sin</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>&#x02218;</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>cos</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>&#x02218;</mo></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>cos</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>&#x02218;</mo></msup></mrow><mrow><mi>sin</mi><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>&#x02218;</mo></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>. All the denominators are nonzero in this range.</p><p>The 88 factors other than <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>tan</mi><msup><mn>45</mn><mo>&#x02218;</mo></msup></mrow></math> form 44 complementary pairs. The unpaired factor is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" display=\"inline\"><mrow><mi>tan</mi><msup><mn>45</mn><mo>&#x02218;</mo></msup><mo>&#x0003D;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></math>, so the product is 1. Answer A.</p>",
  "hints": [
    {
      "title": "Match angles from opposite ends",
      "body": "<p>Use the supplied complementary-angle identity to express a tangent at an angle near the end of the list in terms of the angle paired with it at the beginning.</p>",
      "recap": "Tangent is sine divided by cosine, with nonzero cosine, and exact standard-angle values fix special factors.",
      "pitfall": "If the number of factors is odd, one factor may remain unpaired.",
